{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01166",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.19,
      "end_seconds": 5.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.48,
      "end_seconds": 11.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.63,
      "end_seconds": 18.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Doctor, it's numbness in my feet. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.08,
      "end_seconds": 21.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.4,
      "end_seconds": 31.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "Around about three months... no wait, it's more like six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.28,
      "end_seconds": 42.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.92,
      "end_seconds": 50.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "It's worse with night. It's once or twice a day. Mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.68,
      "end_seconds": 56.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "What about burning pain in your toes, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.98,
      "end_seconds": 68.33,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "Yeah, that too. As for burning pain in my toes, it happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.0,
      "end_seconds": 73.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Alright, have you noticed back pain, weakness or bladder problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.28,
      "end_seconds": 77.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "No, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.29,
      "end_seconds": 85.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.57,
      "end_seconds": 92.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.99,
      "end_seconds": 96.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.81,
      "end_seconds": 100.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.61,
      "end_seconds": 110.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.87,
      "end_seconds": 126.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.86,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.86,
      "end_seconds": 139.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.82,
      "end_seconds": 142.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.68,
      "end_seconds": 146.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.68,
      "end_seconds": 156.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast. It's febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day for the gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.39,
      "end_seconds": 162.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.01,
      "end_seconds": 167.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes. Gout, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.76,
      "end_seconds": 173.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.4,
      "end_seconds": 183.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.55,
      "end_seconds": 209.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.79,
      "text": "Okay: temp 36.7 degrees, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, BP is 115 over 74, pulse is 85 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.16,
      "end_seconds": 215.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.52,
      "end_seconds": 218.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.55,
      "end_seconds": 241.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "The ankle reflexes are reduced and the feeling is dulled below the knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.78,
      "end_seconds": 249.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.95,
      "end_seconds": 267.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, this is probably a peripheral neuropathy, probably related to diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.05,
      "end_seconds": 272.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.78,
      "end_seconds": 296.36,
      "duration_seconds": 18.58,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a peripheral neuropathy, probably related to diabetes is my leading thought, not anything worse. I want an HbA1c done, that's for diabetes. I'm sending you for a B12 level because of neuropathy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.98,
      "end_seconds": 302.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, when would that take place?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.4,
      "end_seconds": 313.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "What I'm giving you is amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night, long term. That's for nerve pain. Check both feet daily and wear well-fitting shoes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.41,
      "end_seconds": 332.63,
      "duration_seconds": 18.22,
      "text": "Sure. Let's hold off on a nerve conduction study for now, and if there's no change next month we can revisit it. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.69,
      "end_seconds": 335.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.21,
      "end_seconds": 338.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}